<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Portuguese Republic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Portugal is a country in Southwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, on the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>, that also includes the archipelagos of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madeira">Madeira</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azores">Azores</a>. Muslims had occupied the peninsula since 711; as a result of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>, Portugal was established as a county of the Kingdom of León in 868 and formally as a kingdom in 1179. In 1385 John of Aviz was elected king and defeated the Castilians. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-discovery">Age of Discovery</a> the kingdom advanced nautical science and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>. It became a republic in 1910 and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> in 1926; the dictatorship was overthrown in 1974 and democracy established in 1976.</p></div>
